## Use

```bash
uv sync
{% if profile == 'report' -%}
uv run {{ project_name }} results.json --out report.md
{%- else -%}
uv run {{ project_name }} --demo    # a random walk: expect no edge (a sanity check)
uv run {{ project_name }} --prices prices.csv --signal momentum --lookback 20
{%- endif %}
```
{%- if profile != 'report' %}

Price files are wide: a `date` column, then one column of prices per asset. Dates are ISO
(`2024-01-09`), unique, and ascending{% if 'data-parquet' in components %}; `.parquet` files work
too, with text or date columns{% endif %}.
{%- if 'data-database' in components %}

### Database

`--database` runs the query in `{{ package_name }}/config.py` against the {{ db_kind }} database
configured there{% if db_read_only == 'yes' %}, read-only{% endif %}. The query must return
`date`, `asset`, and `price` columns. Credentials come from the environment, never from the
project (see `.env.example`):
{%- if db_kind == 'postgres' %}
`DATABASE_PASSWORD` for user `{{ db_user }}`, or a full `DATABASE_URL`. Connections verify the
server certificate (`sslmode={{ db_sslmode }}`); set `PGSSLROOTCERT` to your CA certificate, or
add `sslrootcert=system` to `DATABASE_URL` for a publicly signed server.
{%- else %}
an optional `DATABASE_URL` replaces the file path `{{ db_name }}`.
{%- endif %}

```bash
uv run {{ project_name }} --check-connection   # connect, then exit
uv run {{ project_name }} --database
```
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}

